{"kind":"assert","text":"J4: revoke the independent read token before 19:15:33 EDT, with this script, once. Ruling 92167206 needs a read that fails while the token's own expiry is still ahead, so an expired token proves nothing, and no later phase can repair that.\n\nThe script is `/private/tmp/artroom-j4-provider-channel-inputs-20261031-v16/run-revoke.sh`, read-only, SHA 0513fd4fb5ab847577b1b861f88f24790665a33fa7bcc9a13e7aa9153912a84a. Read it first. I checked its syntax and have not run it.\n\nIt runs `revoke-read`, with the mint-read input, then writes the denied read's input, which adds only the revoke receipt, and runs `revoked-git-read`. It stops unless the read answers 401 or 403 before expiry. Each channel run took about 5 s at 19:00.\n\nThe token has no later use. `operator.mjs:58` says only work reads this custody, and work finished. So run it in whichever gap between phases comes first. Do not run it during a phase's run if your tool runs one command at a time and that would pass 19:15.\n\nIf it stops, tell me the outcome word. `HALTED.json` in `provider-channel-v4-1` then blocks a retry, and the rule in b4ec3cdd holds.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2325d2bdec8bb369d6c3cd77d8163d178ccacc09, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:453535e2fd294d9a0ef7f603f798f6732ecc4cf4 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:043d587ef18b62fdeee6b57f8968de1567206697, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:171f5f57d26458ff1e85c1f9e0a69fefb342bc9b and 19 more"}}